From f8e49fab03e4ef0e294c2d844e4860a0df6ae84b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 18:00:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Harden DPRNT file tailing: tail fingerprint, bounded
 catch-up, safe truncation

Detect rewrites by comparing the bytes just before the consumed offset instead
of the share-cached last-write time; a fresh reader without truncation reads only
the file tail for the current PartName and replays no historical events; never
truncate while a line is unterminated; expose dprnt in the public CNC
configuration; test the DPRNT file in every connection test; mark the DPRNT-only
PartName stale while the source is offline.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JMNbrUi8mkQMTaJDLsmBGe
