@@ -1371,7 +1371,7 @@ The `/haas/*` routes remain compatibility/commissioning endpoints. New monitorin
 
 `dprntPort` defaults to `8080`. With `dprntSource: "TCP"` (default) the Server persistently subscribes to this read-only Haas DPRNT output and accepts a complete part-number-shaped line as the preferred `MachineHeaderPartName`; it never derives Part identity from a filename or O-number. A serial-only controller behind a serial-to-Ethernet bridge in TCP-server mode uses the same source.
 
-`dprntSource: "FILE"` tails a controller-written DPRNT text file at `dprntFilePath` (a UNC path readable by the Server service account), for example the Mazak Matrix `C:\MC_sdg\print\print.txt` produced by DPR14 = 4. Only lines appended since the previous poll are consumed; a file the controller rewrote or shortened is read again from the start; an unterminated last line waits for its terminator. Line semantics are identical to the TCP source (part-number lines and `MEIMAD/` event lines). `dprntFileTruncateAfterRead: true` empties the file after a poll that consumed it completely, only when its length is still exactly what was read, and requires write access; the failure of a truncation is reported in `lastError` without stopping ingestion. An unreadable file marks the `DPRNT` component `UNAVAILABLE` and the connection `DEGRADED` (`OFFLINE` for the `DPRNT` telemetry provider).
+`dprntSource: "FILE"` tails a controller-written DPRNT text file at `dprntFilePath` (a UNC path readable by the Server service account), for example the Mazak Matrix `C:\MC_sdg\print\print.txt` produced by DPR14 = 4. Only lines appended since the previous poll are consumed; a file the controller rewrote or shortened is read again from the start; an unterminated last line waits for its terminator. Line semantics are identical to the TCP source (part-number lines and `MEIMAD/` event lines). A new reader (Server start, reconnect, or connection edit) cannot know which part of an existing file was already ingested: without truncation it reads only the last 64 KB to recover the current PartName and replays no historical `MEIMAD/` events; with truncation enabled everything still in the file is unconsumed by definition and is replayed, so events emitted while the Server was down are not lost. `dprntFileTruncateAfterRead: true` empties the file after a poll that consumed it completely and ended on a line terminator, only when its length is still exactly what was read, and requires write access; the failure of a truncation is reported in `lastError` without stopping ingestion. An unreadable file marks the `DPRNT` component `UNAVAILABLE` and the connection `DEGRADED` (`OFFLINE` for the `DPRNT` telemetry provider).
 
 `telemetryProvider: "DPRNT"` declares a controller with no MDC/MTConnect telemetry (for example Mazak Matrix 2). The snapshot then carries no machine state, active program, or part counter (`UNSUPPORTED`), Part identity comes only from DPRNT lines, `allowWrite` is forced to `false`, and the connection is `ONLINE` once the DPRNT source is readable and a PartName has been seen.
 
