@@ -95,7 +95,9 @@ The active NC program’s machine-side header/DPRNT `PartName` is the authoritat
 
 **DPRNT source = FILE** reads a DPRNT text file that the controller writes itself, over a UNC share. Use it for a Mazak Matrix / Matrix 2 control: set DPR14 = 4 so DPRNT lines go to `C:\MC_sdg\print\print.txt` on the control PC, share that folder read-only for the Server service account, and enter the UNC path (for example `\\MAZAK-VARIAXIS\print\print.txt`) as the DPRNT file path. The Server reads only new lines after each poll and re-reads the file from the start if the control rewrote it. Use **Test DPRNT** to confirm the Server can read the file and to see the last PartName it contains.
 
-No G-code deletes that file. Tick **Clear DPRNT file after each read** if the file must not grow on the control; the Server then empties the file after it has consumed it (the share must allow write access). Leave it unticked if the control keeps the file small itself.
+No G-code deletes that file. Tick **Clear DPRNT file after each read** if the file must not grow on the control; the Server then empties the file after it has consumed it (the share must allow write access), and any `MEIMAD/` events written while the Server was down are still picked up from the file on restart. Leave it unticked if the control keeps the file small itself; the Server then recovers only the current PartName from the end of the file after a restart and does not replay old events.
